Ok...our NetWorker server (5.5.2), which is running on Tru64 5.1 =
patch-kit 3, uses gigabit ethernet to perform the backups of the other =
servers.  Before TU5.1, we had to define the gigabit cards in the =
inet.local file--which worked just fine.  Then when we upgraded to 5.1, =
we decided to use the rc.config instead of the inet.local.  The cards =
continued to work fine for any kind of file transfers we did.  But the =
NetWorker backups would time out on most of the filesets that were being =
backed up.  The weirdest thing is that our biggest single fileset backed =
up fine (about 100GB)--but small ones like / and /usr would fail with a =
timeout exceeded warning. =20
We have an open case with Legato to figure out the problem.  but in the =
meantime what I did last night was to put the gigabit cards back in the =
inet.local file--and the backups completed perfectly.  So my question =
is, has anyone else had a similar problem with NetWorker?  I don't =
really understand it, because the cards seemed to be working fine--no =
collisions or anything like that.  We didn't change any hardware at all =
during this process.  Any suggestions would be much appreciated. =20

Jonathan Williams
UNIX Systems Administrator
The Shubert Organization, Inc.

