Date: Wed, 12 Sep 2001 12:07:37 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Urgent.. Problem with Exporting Clustered file system
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653680321920

Hi Managers,

PROBLEM: 
     The Ase Service gets relocated but the ASE
exported NFS area is not getting exported.

ENVIRONMENT: 
     Member Systems - AS4100 
     OS             - TRU64 v 4.0f
     TruCluster     - v 1.6
     ASE Usage      - NFS Service


PROBLEM DESCRITION:
All service uses the first member as the Favoured
member for serving. This config was being in use
(non-stop) for the last few months and we've had no
problems.

Today, I tried to realocate one of the service to the
second member of the ASE. The service is getting
realocated but the ASE exported NFS Area is not
getting exported. I mean service is not getting
mounted on any of the clients. I tried realocation all
the Nfs services to the next member. The problem
remained the same.

SINCE THE BASIC EXPORTING OF CLUSTERED FILE SYSTEM IS
HAVING PROBLEM EVEN HIGH AVAILABILITY FEATURE IS NOT
WORKING. I MEAN THE FAIL OVER.

ACTION TAKEN:
Removed Cluster (ALL THE SUBSETS RELATED TO CLUSTER)
from both the system without installing the base
operating system. The problem is still the same.
Instaled the following patches related to Trucluster
v1.6 
- TCRPAT00000100160
- TCRPAT00000200160
- TCRPAT00000300160
- TCRPAT00000400160

Thanks in advance.

reg
NG


