From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Sep 10 01:17:41 2001
From: "Loucks, Guy" <Guy.Loucks () det ! nsw ! edu ! au>
Date: Mon, 10 Sep 2001 01:17:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary RE: TC5.1 Cluster creation items with LSM...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653680321880

People,

My apologies in the delay for this summary. The server is now stable.

A few questions were raised about LSM, even though we have a rootdg, the O/S
root is not involved with this.

There seems to be some issues with LSM, and I believe there is a case logged
with this. The work around, and this is NOT PRETTY:

In non-cluster:
VOLDG DEPORT - export the old file system

Boot Cluster in single user, bcheckrc ignore lsm errors, get all the errors
about on-line aliased,...

edit /sbin/lsm-startup
change:
newton {root}>grep -i "\-k" lsm-startup
#vold_opts=-k
vold_opts="-k -x noloadbalance -x noautoconfig"

Now we need to tell it is a version 4, so we need to create a volboot file:

VOLDCTL ADD DISK DSK..e This is the disk with your LSM database region
(private?)

RE-BOOT into full cluster

VOLDCTL ADD DISK DSK... This is to tell LSM about the disks in the other
datadg.

VOLDG -o CONVERT_OLD -o SHARED IMPORT DATADG

Check your fsets, re-boot, and the cluster is now happy.

This is as elegant as a Mack truck in a fine china shop, but it does appear
to work.

Regards,

Guy




