To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Login problems
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653680321860


Hi!

We have an AS1200 here running Tru64 V5.1 which are experiencing some
strange problems.

This Monday the machine suddenly stopped accepting logins (telnet, ssh,
su, CDE). The prompt would just hang instead. A reboot would lead to the
CDE-login screen not starting up ok. After Compaq had unsuccessfully tried
to fix the problem we replaced the system disk and the machine would run
without problems for about 40 odd hours. Then it happened again.

Anyone who has experienced this before and/or knows a solution to it? No
system resource (memory, swap, disk, pttys) seem to be exhausted and
kernel parametres have been raised to quite high values. We normally have
150 - 300 simultaneous users on the machine and haven't experienced these
problems before..

/Eskil

