From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Sep 06 13:51:34 2001
From: Gary Mulder <gary () cgen ! com>
Date: Thu, 06 Sep 2001 13:51:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary 2: Maximum disk partition size in Tru64 V5.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653680321839

All,

Just a follow-on summary to my previous summary. Kevin Partin from Compaq
corrected my previous summary in that the maximum volume (partition) size that
V5.1 supports is 1TB-512K :

	http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/pub_page/spds.html

This was evidenced as we started observing write errors when writing to a
single monolithic 1.4TB partition :

 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix: AdvFS I/O error:
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Domain#Fileset: raid2_dmn#raid2_fs
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Mounted on: /abcd 
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Volume: /dev/disk/dsk11c
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Tag: 0x00000177.800b
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Page: 0
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Block: 2147998080
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Block count: 16
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Type of operation: Write
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     Error: 30
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     EEI: 0x200
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     To obtain the name of the file on which
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     the error occurred, type the command:
 Aug 23 12:20:02 abcd vmunix:     /sbin/advfs/tag2name /abcd /.tags/375

On repartitioning it into two 700GB LUNs we did not see these write errors. To
get a single 1.4TB file set we would then need to then combine these two 700GB
volumes into one file set using addvol from the "ADVFS-UTILITIES PAK" (which of
course we don't have).

Gary

