software did the trick. the general "broadcast" feature didn't work, but
I used the option of pointing it at my Alpha/Tru64 server and the CDE
login box comes up in its own window. It also now disconnects cleanly.
thanks to all who responded.

kevin

Kevin McGrath wrote:
> 
> howdy,
> 
> I wanted to run CDE on my NT workstation from my tru64 server run v4.0f.
> we were able to get it running by starting my excursion software on my
> NT box and then telneting to the unix server, doing a setenv DISPLAY
> node:0, and then running the "/usr/dt/bin/dtsession" program. this
> allows the CDE to startup but it doesn't logoff gracefully and I have to
> restart my eXcursion server to make the CDE windows go away.
> 
> this all seems kinda awkward so I'm wondering who has been down this
> path before and found a better way?
> 
